{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the earth brought forth vegetation.</b> And it did not say 'and Elohim made — every tree making fruit after its kind, and the vegetation after its kind' — because it is not fitting to mention the name Elohim in connection with the possessors of the vegetative soul, which is not as distinguished as the soul of motion, of which it did mention the name Elohim, for it says: ״ויעש אלהים את חית הארץ״ — 'and Elohim made the beast of the earth' — because the soul of motion serves the rational soul in many ways, but the vegetative soul has no importance except the importance of the body, and it serves only the body alone, for the soul has no need to grow:" "<b>And if</b> you consider it, you will find that Scripture mentioned five species of plant life, and they are: 'let the earth sprout vegetation' (תדשא הארץ דשא); 'herb yielding seed' (עשב מזריע זרע); 'fruit tree' (עץ פרי) — the taste of the tree being like the taste of the fruit; 'making fruit' (עושה פרי) — that is, the fruit itself, which has its seed within it — behold, five." "<b>And you should be roused</b> to reflect that all number is included in three, for you will not find any number except either one, or a pair, or an odd number; and the number three includes them all, for it contains one — which is the one — and it contains a pair — which is the two — and it contains an odd number, which is three. And it is well known that the number three is the divider of the one, just as the number four is the divider of the two. And because the number three is the divider of the one, which is hidden, therefore the created beings up to the third day were stored away and hidden — for the light that was created on the first day was stored away from the creatures; also the firmament that was created on the second day, and also the trees of Eden that were created on the third, were stored away from the creatures. And everything that was made up to the third day is called 'world' (עולם), because it is hidden (נעלם); and what was made after it, on the fourth day, is called 'year' (שנה); and the reason is that just as three is the divider of the one, so four is the divider of the two, for four is nothing but the doubling of two. Therefore the two luminaries, which are of the power of twoness, were created on the fourth day, which is the double of two; and the year is called 'year' (שנה) because it is completed by these two luminaries. And for this reason they were suspended in that firmament that was created on the second day, which is of the power of twoness — and it is that which divides between waters and waters — for so the luminaries were fixed in it to divide between the day and the night and between the light and the darkness. And everything that was made after it, on the fifth day and on the sixth day, is what is called 'soul' (נפש), and this is what is mentioned in Sefer Yetzirah: 'world, year, soul' (עולם שנה נפש)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:25:01.791402825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}